00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:50.000
not to speak to the media, in a bid to raise awareness, Colin and Diane invited members of the press into their home to make a public appeal for information. They said they hadn't been able to sleep, spending many hours with police going over Louise's photographs, school reports, and anything at all that might provide some sort of clue. Sitting solemnly on the couch in their lounge room, an emotionally distraught Colin Bell broke down in tears as he told TV news reporters, I'm convinced she's not hiding anywhere, and if someone is watching this, don't harm her, please don't. Diane sat by his side, visibly shaken as she timidly asked her daughter to

