discovery of Louise's earrings was once again involuntarily involved with the investigation. The woman awoke at 6.45 am and went to collect the milk and newspaper from her front yard when she noticed what appeared to be an old rag laying on her lawn. She paid the item no attention and carried on with her morning routine. Hours later, at around 9 am, she returned home after dropping her son off at school when the rag caught her sight once more as she noticed that was neatly folded. She picked it up and realized it wasn't a rag at all, but a sleeveless cotton pajama top dotted with yellow flowers. It had multiple tears down each side and was drenched in water.

