00:24:19.000 --> 00:25:06.000
put his own safety at risk, Father Aiken replied, I have no dependence. This girl is just beginning life and I don't mind putting myself in danger if it's going to help someone. Father Aiken's invitation yielded no response. Meanwhile, police continued with their investigation, door knocking over 2,500 homes and conducting interviews with over 8,000 people. Despite these efforts, months passed with no compelling leads or discoveries. Then, crucial information was offered from an unexpected source, when several inmates at the now defunct Adelaide Jail alleged they knew who was responsible

